※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=3031

※ Several things stand where one is written -- which is a thing only an argument
※ list has room for.  Anywhere else exactly one value is wanted, so the glyph
※ would have to mean something else, and there is nothing for it to mean.  It is
※ therefore not an expression at all, which is why the parser says this rather
※ than the checker.

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let p: 〈u8, u8〉 = 〈1u8, 2u8〉
    let q: 〈u8, u8〉 = ⁂p
    q⟦0⟧
